<h2>Attributes of Other Quadrilaterals</h2>
<p>Practice the source's four division-by-seven mental facts, then inspect all six original labelled figures and choose <strong>every</strong> valid shape name. Explain each decision to your teacher. Shape 6 is a rotated square: rotation never changes its side lengths or right angles.</p>
<p><a href="https://cms-assets.illustrativemathematics.org/f7p5ykdvdzqxa4est0ezo494xyay" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the original 2021 Student Task Statements PDF (7 pages)</a> — original figures and dot grids are viewed at the publisher, not copied into Edulytics.</p>
<table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Shape family</th><th>Defining attribute</th><th>Important overlap</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Quadrilateral</th><td>Four straight sides</td><td>Includes all rectangles, rhombuses and squares</td></tr>
<tr><th>Rectangle</th><td>Four right angles</td><td>Includes squares</td></tr>
<tr><th>Rhombus</th><td>Four equal-length sides</td><td>Includes squares</td></tr>
<tr><th>Square</th><td>Four right angles AND four equal-length sides</td><td>Both rectangle and rhombus</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Open tasks — teacher review required</h3>
<p>Construct one quadrilateral that is not square; one that is not rhombus; one that is not rectangle; and several that are none of these three types. Show side/angle evidence and compare with a partner (source MLR8). You can submit your explanation below, but this page does not automatically grade drawings.</p>
<p>The publisher's gated Cool-down is not reproduced. The independent Edulytics exit prompt is separate.</p>
